  {
   "id": "P5L0wO1QAgAJ",
   "from": "Arathi Bhaskar",
   "author": "9e9a5575f868c39b",
   "date": "2019-08-14T13:57:46Z",
   "subject": "Binary endogenous variable threshold interpretation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi ,</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I was wondering if anyone could please help me with an interpretation. I am new to SEM and lavaan and any help would be welcome.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">How can I interpret the threshold coefficient of a 0-1 binary endogenous variable in lavaan? Is it the intercept of the probit regression?  The model and part of the  lavaan output is pasted below.  How can I interpret Y2|t1? </p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Many thanks,</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Arathi</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">model1&lt;-&#39;</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">#measurement model</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Y1 =~ z1 + z2 + z3 + z4 + z5</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">#structural model</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Y2 ~  b1*Y1 + + c1*X1+\r\nc2*X2 + c3*X3 + b2*M  + X4 + X5</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">M ~ a2*X2 + a3*X3 </p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Y1 ~ a1*X1<br>\r\n&#39;</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">fit1&lt;- sem(model1, data = w1.2,  meanstructure = TRUE, estimator = &quot;WLSMV&quot;,\r\nordered=c(&quot;Y2&quot;, &quot;z1&quot;, &quot;z2&quot;, &quot;z3&quot;,\r\n&quot;z4&quot;,&quot;z5&quot;))</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">z1-z5 are binary, 0-1.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Y2 is binary, M, X1, X2 and X3,  are continuous.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">As part of the output I have:</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\">Thresholds:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\">                   Estimate  Std.Err \r\nz-value  P(&gt;|z|)   Std.lv \r\nStd.all<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\">    z1|t1       \r\n  -0.341   \r\n0.119   -2.875    0.004  \r\n-0.341   -0.341<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\">    z2|t1          -0.584    0.116  \r\n-5.042    0.000   -0.584  \r\n-0.584<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\">    z3|t1     \r\n    -0.807   \r\n0.128   -6.283    0.000  \r\n-0.807   -0.807<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\">    z4|t1   \r\n       0.239   \r\n0.113    2.119    0.034   \r\n0.239    0.239<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\">    z5|t1  \r\n       -0.222   \r\n0.112   -1.976    0.048  \r\n-0.222   -0.222<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\">    Y2|t1          -0.908    0.264  \r\n-3.442    0.001   -0.908  \r\n-0.898<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "llyUH9xkAgAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2019-08-14T20:03:00Z",
   "subject": "Re: Binary endogenous variable threshold interpretation",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">How can I interpret the threshold coefficient of a 0-1 binary endogenous variable in lavaan? Is it the intercept of the probit regression?  </p></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>No, it is -1 times the intercept, if the intercept were estimated and threshold fixed to zero (instead of vice versa, the default).  </div><div><br></div><div>It is the value of the &quot;latent item-response&quot; above which respondents respond 1, but below which respondents respond 0.</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://www.statmodel.com/download/webnotes/CatMGLong.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.statmodel.com/download/webnotes/CatMGLong.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422006695000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3KbFLXS5N35ZJgrWH9x45h\">https://www.statmodel.com/download/webnotes/CatMGLong.pdf</a><br></div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080/10705510701758406\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.1080/10705510701758406&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422006695000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0WFR3fZUrOGy2fTRjCkTBe\">https://doi.org/10.1080/10705510701758406</a><br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Terrence D. Jorgensen<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422006695000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2-pWi8-ute7Cvne5CLhCl_\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a><u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><br></div></div><div style=\"font-size:small\"></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
