   "date": "2020-04-14T19:08:58Z",
   "subject": "Re: Binary endogenous variable threshold interpretation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Can these thresholds be thought of as item difficulties like the would in IRT?</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Wednesday, August 14, 2019 at 4:03:00 PM UTC-4, Terrence Jorgensen wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">How can I interpret the threshold coefficient of a 0-1 binary endogenous variable in lavaan? Is it the intercept of the probit regression?  </p></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>No, it is -1 times the intercept, if the intercept were estimated and threshold fixed to zero (instead of vice versa, the default).  </div><div><br></div><div>It is the value of the &quot;latent item-response&quot; above which respondents respond 1, but below which respondents respond 0.</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://www.statmodel.com/download/webnotes/CatMGLong.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.statmodel.com/download/webnotes/CatMGLong.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422006697000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0uvn8HFa8Eu95tBbTfShNW\">https://www.statmodel.com/download/webnotes/CatMGLong.pdf</a><br></div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080/10705510701758406\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.1080/10705510701758406&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422006697000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0NCsB2Bl3lt6tkPKuYbxMU\">https://doi.org/10.1080/10705510701758406</a><br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Terrence D. Jorgensen<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422006697000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3F7-Pj4FhBeISITnWUzvaP\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a><u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><br></div></div><div style=\"font-size:small\"></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
