  {
   "id": "dANKwBk6AQAJ",
   "from": "Hugo Harada",
   "author": "73fb61795976b321",
   "date": "2020-04-14T19:58:43Z",
   "subject": "Re: Binary endogenous variable threshold interpretation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">Thresholds are related to the &quot;d&quot; and &quot;a&quot; IRT parameters through the equations listed in the mentioned paper. They related to the &quot;b&quot; parameter by d=-ab. Thus, b (difficulty parameter) depends on both thresholds and loadings...</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><div><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/attach/13a19c04a0374/image.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"image.png\" width=\"562\" height=\"295\"><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><a href=\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/10705510701758406\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/10705510701758406&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422006699000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1bxu-2gd0NZP8cQvLW9Olp\">https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/10705510701758406</a> </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"> <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">Regards,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">Hugo</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">Em ter., 14 de abr. de 2020 às 16:09, Gena Sbeglia &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gena.s...@stonybrook.edu</a>&gt; escreveu:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Can these thresholds be thought of as item difficulties like the would in IRT?<div><br><br>On Wednesday, August 14, 2019 at 4:03:00 PM UTC-4, Terrence Jorgensen wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">How can I interpret the threshold coefficient of a 0-1 binary endogenous variable in lavaan? Is it the intercept of the probit regression?  </p></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>No, it is -1 times the intercept, if the intercept were estimated and threshold fixed to zero (instead of vice versa, the default).  </div><div><br></div><div>It is the value of the &quot;latent item-response&quot; above which respondents respond 1, but below which respondents respond 0.</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://www.statmodel.com/download/webnotes/CatMGLong.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.statmodel.com/download/webnotes/CatMGLong.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422006700000&amp;usg=AOvVaw19LPMSj7OvcUMnbxUwPvvR\">https://www.statmodel.com/download/webnotes/CatMGLong.pdf</a><br></div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080/10705510701758406\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.1080/10705510701758406&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422006700000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3IXTrZYq9I6epEkAEeWYDG\">https://doi.org/10.1080/10705510701758406</a><br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Terrence D. Jorgensen<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792422006700000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0IXn66Rl5iULQF64MO09R2\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a><u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><br></div></div><div style=\"font-size:small\"></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
    ],
